Luca, played by Baird Wallace.

13
01:24:30,000 --> 01:24:36,000
Tea with Mussolini (Italian: Un tè con Mussolini) is a 1999 semi-autobiographical comedy-drama war film directed by Franco Zeffirelli, scripted by John
Mortimer, telling the story of a young Italian boy's upbringing by a circle of British and American women before and during the Second World War.

14
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
At the 53rd British Academy Film Awards, Tea with Mussolini won the BAFTA
Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role (Maggie Smith).

15
01:37:30,000 --> 01:37:36,000
The film also nominated for BAFTA Award for Best
Costume Design but lost to Sleepy Hollow.

16
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,000
The film explores themes of hotel, ambassador, loss of loved one, italy, widow.

17
01:50:30,000 --> 01:50:36,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
